### Orphan Files Deleted
| File | Reason |
|------|--------|
| templates/old_config.j2.j2 | No task references this template |

### Duplicate Code Consolidated
| Files | Consolidated To | Reason |
|-------|-----------------|--------|
| task_a.yml + task_b.yml | task_common.yml | Identical logic |

### Impact
- Files deleted: X
- Variables removed: Y
- Lines of code reduced: Z

### Verification
- `make check-syntax`: PASSED
- `make check-<role>`: PASSED
```

## Safety Checklist

Before removing ANYTHING:
- [ ] Grep for all references across project
- [ ] Check group_vars and host_vars for usage
- [ ] Review git history for context
- [ ] Check if part of public API (documented variables)
- [ ] Run `make check-syntax`
- [ ] Run `make check-<role>` dry-run
- [ ] Create backup branch

After each removal:
- [ ] `make check-syntax` passes
- [ ] `make check-<role>` dry-run passes
- [ ] No broken references
- [ ] Commit changes
- [ ] Update DELETION_LOG.md

## Common Patterns to Remove

### 1. Unused Default Variables
```yaml
# defaults/main.yml - if never referenced elsewhere
old_feature_enabled: false  # Remove this
```

### 2. Commented-Out Code
```yaml
# Remove blocks of commented-out tasks/variables
# - name: Old task
#   ansible.builtin.debug:
#     msg: "This is no longer used"
```

### 3. Redundant Variable Definitions
```yaml
# If value is same as defaults/main.yml, remove from vars/
# vars/main.yml:
nodejs_version: "22.x"  # Same as defaults - redundant
```

### 4. Orphan Templates
```bash
# Template exists but no task uses it:
# templates/old_template.j2 (no reference in tasks/)
```

## When NOT to Use This Agent

- During active feature development
- Right before production deployment
- When role is unstable
- Without proper test coverage
- On code you don't understand

**Remember**: Dead code is technical debt. Regular cleanup keeps the codebase maintainable. But safety first - never remove code without understanding why it exists.
